"Counterexamples to the Balogh-Linz-Patkós Conjecture | Search arXiv (https://searcharxiv.org/abs/2607.03026)\nciteturn2search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4 months ago; Crawled: last week; Balogh, Linz and Patkós (Combinatorial Theory, 2023) conjectured an extremal result for $t$-intersecting $k$-Sperner families when $n+t$ is odd. ... Counterexamples to the Balogh-Linz-Patkós Conjecture. https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.03026\n\narXiv · 2607.03026\n\n# Counterexamples to the Balogh-Linz-Patkós Conjecture\n\nJia-Bao Yang·Leilei Zhang\n\nView original source ↗Read source document ↗Export metadata ↓\n\n## Abstract\n\nA set system $\\mathcal{F}$ is called $t$-intersecting if $|A\\cap B|\\ge t$ for every pair of sets $A,B\\in \\mathcal{F}.$ A set system $\\mathcal{F}$ is $k$-Sperner if it does not contain a chain of length $k+1$. Balogh, Linz and Patkós (Combinatorial Theory, 2023) conjectured an extremal result for $t$-intersecting $k$-Sperner families when $n+t$ is odd. In this note we give an explicit construction that is $t$-intersecting and $k$-Sperner, and whose size exceeds that of the conjectured fixed-star construction for infinitely many values of $n$. Consequently, we disprove the Balogh-Linz-Patkós conjecture for all $t\\ge 2$ and $k\\ge 2$ satisfying $k(t-1)\\ge t+1$.\n\n## Explore related subjects\n\nmath.CO\n\nRECORD DETAILS\n\nSource\n    arXiv\nPublication date\n    2026-07-03\nSource updated\n    2026-07-07\nReuse permissions\n    http://arxiv.org/licenses/nonexclusive-distrib/1.0/\n\nMetadata is provided by the original archive. This page does not imply that the source document or image is freely reusable.\n\nJia-Bao Yang, Leilei Zhang. 2026-07-03. Counterexamples to the Balogh-Linz-Patkós Conjecture. https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.03026--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCounterexamples to the Balogh-Linz-Patkós Conjecture | Request PDF (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/408520494_Counterexamples_to_the_Ba